---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | Amber Uncut"
  description="What Amber Uncut collects, what it does not, and how to get your information removed."
>
  <SiteHeader />

  <main>
    <article class="full-story" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
      <div class="story-kicker"><span>PRIVACY</span><span>PLAIN ENGLISH</span></div>
      <h1 id="privacy-title">The <em>short version.</em></h1>
      <div class="full-story-copy">
        <p>
          I am a barber, not a data company. This site collects as little as possible, and I am not
          selling anything about you to anyone.
        </p>

        <h2>What I collect</h2>
        <p>
          If you type your email into the signup form, I keep that email so I can send you a note
          when I write something. That is it. No name, no address, no tracking of what you read.
        </p>

        <h2>What I do not collect</h2>
        <p>
          There are no advertising trackers, no cookies set by me, and no analytics watching where
          you click. I do not know who you are unless you tell me.
        </p>

        <h2>Other companies involved</h2>
        <p>
          This site is hosted by GitHub Pages, which keeps basic server logs like IP addresses for
          security purposes. The fonts come from Google Fonts, and the icons from a service called
          unpkg. Those requests reach their servers when your browser loads the page. If you sign up
          for the email list, the form provider stores your address so I can reach you.
        </p>

        <h2>Getting removed</h2>
        <p>
          Message me on <a href={SITE.instagram} rel="me noopener" target="_blank">Instagram</a> or
          reach me through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> and ask me to delete your email.
          I will, and I will not ask you why.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>This site is meant for adults and is not directed at children under 13.</p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If this ever changes, for example if I add sponsors or analytics, I will update this page
          to say so plainly.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
